WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:04.860
The Red Face Demon is an evil entity&nbsp;
who may be as ancient as time itself. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:07.968
resides in a netherworld, another plane&nbsp;
separate from the land of the living.

00:00:07.968 --> 00:00:13.740
– [Specs] Does this other plane have a name?
– [Elise] Let’s call it… The Further.

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:17.520
– It’s possible that the demon came about&nbsp;
in the 1700s, which is when historians&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:21.420
believe the first modern carnival originated&nbsp;
in the Caribbean, because Insidious director&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:24.480
James Wan has described the demon’s&nbsp;
appearance as something out of a crazy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:28.860
mystical carnival. The tufts of hair protruding&nbsp;
from the side of the head and razor sharp teeth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:33.300
do bear a resemblance to another terrifying&nbsp;
carnival entity from another plane of existence:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:38.040
Pennywise. However, other demons in the franchise&nbsp;
have the ability to change their appearance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:40.560
so it’s possible that this demon is much older.

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:44.400
But Red Face’s confinement to The Further&nbsp;
would not last forever. One of the main&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:48.480
ideas expressed in the franchise is the inherent&nbsp;
risk that comes with exploring the other world.

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:53.760
– I’ve been to that dark place&nbsp;
too. It’s not a place for pure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:58.200
souls. It is very dangerous. Things come back with you.

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:01.920
– [Zac] And I believe that’s exactly what&nbsp;
happened when psychic medium Elise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:05.880
Rainier entered The Further in about&nbsp;
2007. I’m guessing the year based on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:09.060
the fact that Insidious Chapter 3 takes&nbsp;
place a few years before the first film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:13.920
and the main character Quinn has a T-Mobile&nbsp;
Sidekick 3, which came out in July 2006.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:17.220
Quinn’s family isn’t doing well, so it&nbsp;
makes sense she’d have last year's model.

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:21.360
Quinn ends up getting stranded in The Further&nbsp;
by another demon, and Elise has to come out of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:25.740
retirement to rescue her. It seems that all is&nbsp;
well after this, but Elise does not immediately&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:30.300
realize what came back with her. She gets home&nbsp;
to find her late husband’s vest on the bed, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:35.940
at first, believes it was his spirit who placed&nbsp;
it there. Then she notices a face in the closet.

00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:42.746
(dog barking)

00:01:42.746 --> 00:01:44.554
(stinger)

00:01:44.554 --> 00:01:48.420
To learn how this entity became attached to the&nbsp;
Lambert family, what the demon is supposed to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:53.160
represent and how its presence can still be felt&nbsp;
today, stick around to the end of this video.

00:01:53.447 --> 00:01:55.447
This video is sponsored by Factor.

00:01:55.447 --> 00:01:57.447
(metal music)

00:02:01.208 --> 00:02:03.365
Welcome to Horror History. Today&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.365 --> 00:02:07.380
I’m analyzing what most people consider the&nbsp;
main antagonist of the Insidious franchise.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:11.640
In the film, he’s referred to as The Man With&nbsp;
Fire on His Face, but in the end credits,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:15.540
he’s tagged as Lipstick-Face Demon. However&nbsp;
this seems to be more of a nickname created&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:18.780
by the filmmakers because of the way that&nbsp;
the special effects makeup was applied.

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:21.720
– [Wan] The reason he’s called the Lipstick face demon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:24.960
is because he literally paints&nbsp;
his face with a red lipstick.

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:29.100
– So many fans just refer to the character&nbsp;
as The Red Face Demon. In addition to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:32.940
Pennywise similarity I already mentioned,&nbsp;
Red Face seems to be an amalgamation of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:36.420
the scariest parts of many horrors in&nbsp;
cinema. The obvious one that comes to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:39.720
mind is Darth Maul from Star Wars: The&nbsp;
Phantom Menace, whose most iconic scene&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:43.500
takes place at the end of a hallway of red&nbsp;
light, not unlike the demon in Insidious.

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:47.940
Red Face also has long claw-like hands,&nbsp;
reminiscent of Freddy Krueger from A Nightmare&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:52.020
on Elm Street. Freddy is known for haunting&nbsp;
characters in their dreams, and before Dalton&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:55.800
learns about astral projection in Insidious,&nbsp;
he believes The Further to be a dream world.

00:02:55.800 --> 00:03:01.260
The character also possesses a black body, a tail,&nbsp;
a forked tongue, and fur around his hooved feet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:04.800
giving off similarities to traditional&nbsp;
depictions of Satan. The Further is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:08.220
stated to be a limbo that exists before&nbsp;
a ghost moves on, so it’s possible that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:11.400
The Red Faced demon is supposed to be&nbsp;
The Further equivalent of The Devil.

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:14.520
The character is played by Joseph&nbsp;
Bishara. If that name sounds familiar,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:18.900
it’s either because he’s also the composer of&nbsp;
the film’s score, or because you recognize him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:23.580
from other roles he’s played, such as Bathsheba in&nbsp;
The Conjuring or Malthus in the Annabelle films,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.580 --> 00:03:26.580
both of which I’ve already covered&nbsp;
on Horror History. Who would have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:29.280
thought a composer would be the most&nbsp;
frequent actor covered on this show?

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:32.160
To understand how his character&nbsp;
became attached to the Lambert family,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:35.880
we’ve got to take it back to Elise’s&nbsp;
most personal investigation yet.

00:03:36.143 --> 00:03:39.596
(ominous freaking music)

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:46.140
In 2010, a few years into Elise’s partnership with&nbsp;
Specs and Tucker of Spectral-Sightings.com, she’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.140 --> 00:03:50.460
called back to her home town in New Mexico to deal&nbsp;
with a demon who haunted her all the way back in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.460 --> 00:03:54.840
her youth. It pulls her into The Further, but she&nbsp;
defeats it with the help of her mother and nieces.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:59.100
Little does she know, they are being followed by&nbsp;
The Red Face demon, or something to that effect.

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:03.720
As they make their way out of the dark realm,&nbsp;
they take a wrong turn, and end up in The Further&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:08.700
version of the Lambert family’s attic. The Further&nbsp;
is not bound by time, meaning that wandering souls&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:12.720
can visit events from the past, and possibly the&nbsp;
future, although we’ve yet to see that happen.

00:04:12.720 --> 00:04:17.280
Dalton Lambert is the son of Josh Lambert, who&nbsp;
Elise helped many years ago, and they see him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:21.660
fall off an old ladder. But Elise doesn’t know who&nbsp;
he is yet, and thinks they’ve gone the wrong way.

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:24.840
From Dalton’s perspective in the&nbsp;
real world, he can’t see any of them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.840 --> 00:04:28.020
but he does hear the crackling sound&nbsp;
emitted by the Red Face Demon.

00:04:28.134 --> 00:04:33.000
(crackling sound)

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:36.480
The reason that The Red Face Demon has&nbsp;
stayed with Elise for the last few years&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:40.440
is because of her abilities as a medium.&nbsp;
Although she rarely uses it, she has the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.440 --> 00:04:45.060
ability to astral project. She can project her&nbsp;
spirit out of her body and into The Further. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:49.020
demon’s goal is to possess the bodies of the&nbsp;
living. Most non-living entities crave life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.020 --> 00:04:53.760
but Elise later explains that this Demon wants&nbsp;
to possess a body simply to cause pain to others.

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:58.680
When the demon sees Dalton, it realizes that he&nbsp;
too has the ability to astral project, and sees&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.680 --> 00:05:03.120
him as an easier target because of his naivety&nbsp;
as a kid. Dalton believes his astral projection&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:08.280
is just a fun dream, so he’s not afraid to venture&nbsp;
deep into The Further, thus leaving his body as an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:12.960
open vessel for an evil spirit to try to possess.&nbsp;
Because of this, Red Face sticks with Dalton,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.960 --> 00:05:17.640
and coaxes him further and further into The&nbsp;
Further. See, that’s why they call it that.

00:05:17.640 --> 00:05:21.480
Each demon or major evil entity has their&nbsp;
own space in The Further behind a red door,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:25.680
and these doors can connect different&nbsp;
locations &amp; time periods. Red Face puts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:29.100
a door to his lair right in The Lamberts’&nbsp;
attic, essentially replacing the connection&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:33.120
between their California home and Elise’s&nbsp;
New Mexico home that used to be there.

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:35.580
Perhaps because he was curious&nbsp;
about the noise he heard there,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.580 --> 00:05:38.640
and perhaps partially because he’s been&nbsp;
banned from the attic in real life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.640 --> 00:05:42.540
he visits the location in what he thinks&nbsp;
is his dream, and goes far enough into the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.540 --> 00:05:46.260
demon’s lair to discover this horse statue,&nbsp;
which he draws a picture of when he wakes up.

00:05:46.260 --> 00:05:50.040
Dalton also sees Red Face at some point&nbsp;
and draws pictures of him as well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.040 --> 00:05:54.360
in addition to the red doors. This picture&nbsp;
shows it standing at the semicircle shaped&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.360 --> 00:05:57.360
window next to the spinning machine&nbsp;
that it uses to sharpen its claws.

00:05:57.360 --> 00:06:00.300
It’s possible that Dalton was at&nbsp;
first intrigued by this brightly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.300 --> 00:06:03.300
colored new friend, and went deeper&nbsp;
and deeper into The Further to try to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:06.900
get a look at him. Director James Wan and&nbsp;
screenwriter Leigh Whannel allude to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.900 --> 00:06:09.960
idea that his appearance is supposed&nbsp;
to be inviting to children at first.

00:06:09.960 --> 00:06:15.120
– [Wan] It’s kind of like a clown. It’s his twisted&nbsp;
way of trying to make himself look like a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:20.160
good happy person to try to entice you to him.
– [Whannel] He’s the one who’s out there trying to suck&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.160 --> 00:06:24.480
in the spirits of innocent people, especially&nbsp;
children; try and get them out of their bodies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:28.200
draw them out into The Further so he&nbsp;
can then go in and inhabit their body.

00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:32.520
– In my opinion, it didn’t work. He’s just straight&nbsp;
up terrifying, but this is a horror movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.520 --> 00:06:36.360
and that’s a good thing. The music he listens&nbsp;
to also plays into the idea that he’s trying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.360 --> 00:06:40.200
to entice Dalton. His favorite song is&nbsp;
“Tiptoe Through the Tulips” by Tiny Tim.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.200 --> 00:06:44.880
You can imagine a kid being drawn in by the&nbsp;
silly falsetto vocals and ukulele strums,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:49.380
but once you get into the demon’s lair and hear it&nbsp;
echoing through an empty realm of tortured souls,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.380 --> 00:06:54.000
you start to realize, “oh yeah, this song is&nbsp;
creepy AF.” In an interview with The Film Stage,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:56.640
James Wan refers to it as “serial killer music.”

00:06:56.640 --> 00:07:00.720
It would not be long before Dalton began&nbsp;
referring to these “dreams” as “nightmares”,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:04.440
and eventually he’d find himself in one&nbsp;
nightmare he could not wake up from.

00:07:04.627 --> 00:07:06.627
(real big impact sound)

