00:08:15.499 --> 00:08:18.973
(suspenseful music)

00:08:18.973 --> 00:08:22.920
Josh and Renai Lambert have just moved into&nbsp;
their new home with their three children when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.920 --> 00:08:27.060
strange things start to occur. In reality, I can’t&nbsp;
tell you if The Red Face Demon is responsible,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.060 --> 00:08:31.980
or if it was just one of the many ghosts attracted&nbsp;
to Dalton, seeking a human body to inhabit.

00:08:31.980 --> 00:08:36.300
Something moves some of Renai’s books, there’s&nbsp;
a breathing sound heard in the house (which may&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.300 --> 00:08:39.840
just be a draft), a furnace turns on in&nbsp;
the attic all on its own, and the attic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.840 --> 00:08:44.160
door opens without anyone touching it. That one&nbsp;
probably was the demon, trying to lure Dalton&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.160 --> 00:08:48.360
up the stairs. Renai’s sheet music also goes&nbsp;
missing and she finds it in that same attic.

00:08:48.360 --> 00:08:51.600
Finally, the ladder breaks under&nbsp;
Dalton, and although he’s OK at first,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.600 --> 00:08:56.400
the next morning he doesn’t wake up. In reality,&nbsp;
the fall is not what hurt him. That night he went&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.400 --> 00:09:00.600
too deep into the demon’s lair and was captured&nbsp;
and chained up to some kind of demonic shrine.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:04.140
With him trapped in The Further, the demon,&nbsp;
or any of the other spirits that have shown&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.140 --> 00:09:07.680
up at the house would have an opportunity&nbsp;
to take possession of the vacant vessel.

00:09:07.680 --> 00:09:11.880
Three months go by, and Dalton still appears&nbsp;
to be in a coma. He’s living at home off&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.880 --> 00:09:15.780
of IVs. Renai is working downstairs when&nbsp;
she hears something in the baby monitor.

00:09:15.880 --> 00:09:17.454
(whispers)

00:09:17.454 --> 00:09:19.454
– (whispered) He won't wake up.

00:09:22.574 --> 00:09:24.952
There’s nothing you can do.

00:09:24.952 --> 00:09:29.449
– [Zac] The voice says “he won’t wake up. There’s&nbsp;
nothing you can do.” Again, it isn’t clear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.520 --> 00:09:34.380
if this is Red Face himself, or one of the other&nbsp;
spirits. What is clear, is what this voice wants.

00:09:34.466 --> 00:09:35.756
– I want it.

00:09:36.001 --> 00:09:37.719
Kill.  Kill.

00:09:37.719 --> 00:09:42.180
I want it. I want it! NOW!

00:09:42.180 --> 00:09:46.620
– The Lamberts’ other son, Foster, becomes&nbsp;
afraid of rooming across the hall from Dalton,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.620 --> 00:09:50.220
because he claims that his brother is walking&nbsp;
around at night, which is most likely a result&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.220 --> 00:09:54.300
of the demon, who can be invisible in the real&nbsp;
world, puppeting his body around the house.

00:09:54.300 --> 00:09:57.000
They also find red handprints on Dalton’s sheets,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:57.000 --> 00:10:01.440
with long pointed fingers. Nick Cave and The&nbsp;
Bad Seeds would have had a field day with this.

00:10:01.440 --> 00:10:05.640
When Red Face first discovers the&nbsp;
unoccupied body, Elise sees it in her dream.

00:10:06.333 --> 00:10:08.358
(JUMP SCARE)

00:10:08.358 --> 00:10:12.360
In the real world, handprints manifest&nbsp;
themselves on the window. Convinced that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:12.360 --> 00:10:16.260
their house is haunted, The Lamberts move again,&nbsp;
but the spirits that haunt the place follow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:20.760
the scent of Dalton’s uninhabited self, and the&nbsp;
paranormal activity continues in the new house.

00:10:20.760 --> 00:10:22.680
As Renai is taking the trash out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.680 --> 00:10:26.820
the evil creature changes her music to&nbsp;
something a little more to its liking.

00:10:26.820 --> 00:10:30.113
♪ piano music ♪
(record scratch)&nbsp;

00:10:30.113 --> 00:10:35.100
♪ Tiptoe, through the window, by the window… ♪

00:10:35.100 --> 00:10:39.000
The grandmother comes to the house and sees&nbsp;
strange things as well. One night she had a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:39.000 --> 00:10:41.460
dream, which was really an out of&nbsp;
body experience into The Further,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.460 --> 00:10:44.640
where she saw the demon in silhouette&nbsp;
while checking on Dalton in his room.

00:10:44.640 --> 00:10:49.020
It told her that it was a visitor, and when&nbsp;
she asked what it wanted, it pointed to Dalton.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.020 --> 00:10:53.640
The next day when telling the story to Josh and&nbsp;
Renai, Red Face makes a more direct appearance.

00:10:55.100 --> 00:10:57.215
(demonic roar) (scream)

00:10:57.215 --> 00:11:01.320
It disappears into Dalton’s room and locks the&nbsp;
door shut as it tears through everything, leaving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:01.320 --> 00:11:05.760
the place in complete disarray with the comatose&nbsp;
boy laying on the ground when they regain entry.

00:11:05.760 --> 00:11:10.080
Having seen enough, they call in Elise,&nbsp;
Specs and Tucker. They bring in something&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:10.080 --> 00:11:13.920
called a tri-field meter, and Tucker picks&nbsp;
up The Red Face Demon’s cracking noises.

00:11:13.920 --> 00:11:16.620
(cracking sounds)

00:11:16.620 --> 00:11:18.540
Then again outside of Foster’s room.

00:11:18.540 --> 00:11:20.820
(cracking sounds)

00:11:20.820 --> 00:11:25.440
And when Elise visits Dalton’s room, she hears&nbsp;
the noises coming from right above his bed.

00:11:25.440 --> 00:11:28.080
(cracking sounds)

00:11:28.080 --> 00:11:31.680
Being the only one able to see the&nbsp;
monster, she describes it to Specs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:31.680 --> 00:11:35.220
who sketches something very similar to&nbsp;
Dalton’s drawings, and is also really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:35.220 --> 00:11:38.460
creepy. After seeing it potentially&nbsp;
speaking to Renai on the baby monitor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:38.460 --> 00:11:42.420
appearing IRL behind Josh, and allowing the&nbsp;
paranormal investigators to make a sketch,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:42.420 --> 00:11:46.260
I don’t think Red Face fears the humans, even&nbsp;
Elise who has the power to see what it’s up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:46.260 --> 00:11:50.460
to. It’s certainly different from James Wan’s&nbsp;
other demon-hunting franchise, The Conjuring,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:50.460 --> 00:11:54.960
where we see the entities try to hide themselves&nbsp;
from the paranormal investigating protagonists.

00:11:54.960 --> 00:11:59.520
Red Face has probably never faced a formidable&nbsp;
foe, and has no reason to be scared of humans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:59.520 --> 00:12:03.420
plus Elise is portrayed to be much less&nbsp;
super-hero-ey than Lorraine Warren,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:03.420 --> 00:12:07.800
and Specs and Tucker combined are still probably&nbsp;
a jack of less trades than Ed Warren is.

00:12:07.800 --> 00:12:12.300
For these reasons, I like these investigators&nbsp;
way more, but that’s neither here nor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:12.300 --> 00:12:15.960
there. Elise explains the nature of&nbsp;
Dalton’s coma in the now famous line…

00:12:15.960 --> 00:12:18.327
– It’s not the house that’s&nbsp;
haunted.

00:12:20.920 --> 00:12:21.769
It’s your son.

00:12:21.840 --> 00:12:26.640
– She goes onto explain that many nearby entities&nbsp;
can smell the open vessel that is Dalton’s body,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:26.640 --> 00:12:29.520
but the demon is the only one who&nbsp;
is *very* close to possessing him.

00:12:29.520 --> 00:12:33.240
The team sets up cameras around where they’ll&nbsp;
be performing a séance, and seem to connect&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:33.240 --> 00:12:37.020
with the boy’s spirit, but he stops talking&nbsp;
when the demon notices what he’s up to,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:37.020 --> 00:12:41.340
and eventually claims that if The Man With Fire&nbsp;
on His Face hears him, he’s going to hurt him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:41.340 --> 00:12:46.080
and not long after, the evil entity hijacks the&nbsp;
communication and berates Elise with obscenities,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:46.080 --> 00:12:49.140
threatening to rip her innards out&nbsp;
and eat the guts that spill from her.

00:12:49.140 --> 00:12:55.920
For the first time in months, Dalton moves.&nbsp;
He appears to sleepwalk over to the group&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:55.920 --> 00:13:01.080
and smack the table, effectively air yeeting&nbsp;
everyone in its vicinity. He also smacks Specs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:01.080 --> 00:13:04.500
sending him flying across the room into&nbsp;
a wall. While it would appear that Dalton&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:04.500 --> 00:13:08.400
has been possessed to do these things, one of&nbsp;
the still frames eventually reveals that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:08.400 --> 00:13:12.240
Red Face Demon was only standing behind&nbsp;
the boy, essentially puppeting his body.

00:13:12.240 --> 00:13:15.420
It takes time for an entity of The&nbsp;
Further to actually possess somebody,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:15.420 --> 00:13:20.040
and Red Face was at the doorstep, but not&nbsp;
quite there. Regardless, Elise’s retaliation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:20.040 --> 00:13:23.820
seemed to do the trick for the time being, and&nbsp;
the demon retreated to its lair to presumably&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:23.820 --> 00:13:28.200
sharpen up its claws one last time before making&nbsp;
an ultimate attempt at taking over Dalton’s body.

00:13:28.200 --> 00:13:32.280
An interesting detail about the lair, is the&nbsp;
demon’s collection of marionettes, which are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:32.280 --> 00:13:36.540
likely symbolic of the way Red Face puppeteered&nbsp;
Dalton’s body during the séance. It seems&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:36.540 --> 00:13:40.620
it was able to do this convincingly because it&nbsp;
practiced to become an expert using these puppets.

00:13:40.620 --> 00:13:45.360
The lair is also decorated with gothic revival&nbsp;
architecture, featuring great chandeliers and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:45.360 --> 00:13:50.280
candelabras, roman looking statues everywhere,&nbsp;
gargoyles, a low lying fog, and giant masks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:50.280 --> 00:13:54.540
looking upwards. The scene was filmed in the&nbsp;
Harold Examiner building in downtown Los Angeles,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:54.540 --> 00:13:58.860
one of the few examples of 100 year old&nbsp;
architecture that still maintains a sheen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:58.860 --> 00:14:03.720
of luxury. Perfect for this demon, who is both&nbsp;
ancient and powerful among the world of demons.

00:14:03.720 --> 00:14:07.920
But the demon’s netherworldian manicure is&nbsp;
interrupted when it notices the spirit of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:07.920 --> 00:14:11.220
Josh Lambert, who has projected into&nbsp;
The Further to try to save his son,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:11.220 --> 00:14:15.180
and the interruption of the Further’s most&nbsp;
nefarious creature would not be welcome.

00:14:15.180 --> 00:14:19.192
(el impacto)

00:14:20.683 --> 00:14:24.000
(tense music)

00:14:24.000 --> 00:14:28.200
After finding out why his son refers&nbsp;
to this demon as The Man With Fire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:28.200 --> 00:14:31.860
In His Face first hand, he’s air yeeted&nbsp;
across the room by the creature’s screech,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:31.860 --> 00:14:36.720
but the distraction allows Dalton, now free&nbsp;
from his chains, to escape. The demon can be seen charging and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:36.720 --> 00:14:41.340
knocking Josh down a second time, he gets to&nbsp;
his feet, scoops up his son and runs for it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:41.340 --> 00:14:44.700
leaving The Red Faced Demon to track&nbsp;
them with its piercing yellow eyes.

00:14:44.700 --> 00:14:49.440
This battle was not over and it’s ferocity was&nbsp;
shaking the entire house back in the real world.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:49.440 --> 00:14:53.700
The father and son find themselves surrounded&nbsp;
by wandering spirits, having called too much&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:53.700 --> 00:14:58.440
attention to themselves, and Josh uses the last of&nbsp;
his energy to get them back to the house. Unable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:58.440 --> 00:15:03.420
to go on, he stops to rest as tell Dalton to go&nbsp;
on ahead to return to his own body, but before the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:03.420 --> 00:15:07.560
boy can get there, he’s ambushed by his demonic&nbsp;
captor, who is waiting for him in his room.

00:15:07.560 --> 00:15:11.820
Dalton flees to his parents room, but Red&nbsp;
Face once again teleports through The Further,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:11.820 --> 00:15:14.580
this time emerging under the bed&nbsp;
to try to drag the child under,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:14.580 --> 00:15:16.620
but he wiggles free and runs down the hall.

00:15:16.620 --> 00:15:21.600
Red Face then unleashes more of his power, by wall&nbsp;
crawling out of the room, the drywall crumbling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:21.600 --> 00:15:25.800
with each step he takes, but he’s unable to&nbsp;
recapture Dalton who makes it back to his physical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:25.800 --> 00:15:30.780
body, closing the door on any chances of being&nbsp;
possessed. The only other available vessel then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:30.780 --> 00:15:34.980
is Josh, who does get partially possessed by&nbsp;
another entity known as The Bride in Black,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:34.980 --> 00:15:39.180
leaving no available landing spot for the&nbsp;
demon with the red face. He can’t even go back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:39.180 --> 00:15:43.980
to stalking Elise, because she is killed by The&nbsp;
Bride in Black, so her body is no longer of use.

00:15:43.980 --> 00:15:48.600
With this development, Red Face seems to just&nbsp;
give up on the Lambert family and move onto&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:48.600 --> 00:15:53.400
a new target, a girl named Allison, who also had&nbsp;
the ability to astral project. Allison was in some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:53.400 --> 00:15:56.940
kind of accident and had to be resuscitated&nbsp;
at the hospital, but while she was out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:56.940 --> 00:16:00.840
she seemingly ventured into The Further, and&nbsp;
brought The Red Face Demon back with her.

00:16:00.840 --> 00:16:04.200
After helping The Lambert family clear&nbsp;
out their evil spirits a second time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:04.200 --> 00:16:08.520
Specs and Tucker visit Allison’s family to try&nbsp;
to offer assistance, with Elise tagging along&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:08.520 --> 00:16:13.140
as a spirit in The Further. When Elise tries to&nbsp;
elicit a response from Allison, she seems to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:13.140 --> 00:16:18.360
as empty of a shell as Dalton once was, and&nbsp;
it’s not long before Elise figures out why…

00:16:18.807 --> 00:16:20.964
(cracking sound)

00:16:20.964 --> 00:16:23.649
– Oh my God…

00:16:23.650 --> 00:16:25.020
(gasp)

00:16:25.020 --> 00:16:27.840
– [Zac] Elise recognizes that sound from the haunting that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:27.840 --> 00:16:31.440
resulted in her losing her own&nbsp;
life. The battle was not over.

00:16:31.440 --> 00:16:36.060
The upcoming Insidious: Fear the Dark (aka:&nbsp;
Chapter 5) will supposedly catch up with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:36.060 --> 00:16:41.040
Lambert family 10 years later. As much as scary&nbsp;
ghosts + scary virus sounds like a terrifying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:41.040 --> 00:16:44.700
combination, I am going to be very frustrated if&nbsp;
we don’t get a follow up on this cliff-hanger.

00:16:44.700 --> 00:16:49.380
However if we do see Darth Maul’s lost cousin&nbsp;
again, I’ll be sure to update this video. Make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:49.380 --> 00:16:52.800
sure you don’t miss that, or any of my&nbsp;
other Insidious character analysis’ by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:52.800 --> 00:16:56.760
subscribing to CZsWorld for new horrors&nbsp;
every week, ringing that death bell for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:56.760 --> 00:17:02.100
all notifications and I will see you in&nbsp;
the next one. Assuming we both survive.

00:17:03.230 --> 00:17:05.230
(urban music)

